  "caption": "Quinn's running group had a secret: little leaks on jumps and hills. Friend Jess had a plan: six toilet stops per 5k, just in case.\n\nLeaking with impact is common in active women, but it isn't something you simply have to put up with. Supervised pelvic floor training has good evidence, and squeezing harder isn't always the answer.\n\nWhat can help: having a pelvic health physio confirm you're using the right muscles, committing for a few months, progressing from lying to standing to impact, easing straining and breath-holding on heavy lifts, and not going \"just in case\".\n\nSee your GP first for blood in your urine, pain passing urine, repeat infections, sudden leaking with no trigger or a dragging heaviness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
